            0.177
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, the point (– 4, 6) divides the line segment joining the points A(– 6, 10) and B(3, – 8) in the ratio 2 : 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.197,
            0.898,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Alternatively :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The ratio "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "m _ { _ 1 } : m _ { _ 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " can also be written as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { m _ { 1 } } { m _ { 2 } } \\colon 1 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , or k : 1. Let (– 4, 6) divide AB internally in the ratio k : 1. Using the section formula, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.272,
            0.897,
            0.32
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "(-4,6)=\\left(\\frac{3k-6}{k+1},\\frac{-8k+10}{k+1}\\right)\\tag{2}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.353,
            0.135,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.426,
            0.341,
            0.565,
            0.382
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "-   4 =   { \\frac { 3 k - 6 } { k + 1 } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.396,
            0.138,
            0.414
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.378,
            0.395,
            0.558,
            0.414
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "-4k-4=3k-6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.421,
            0.139,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.433,
            0.42,
            0.508,
            0.439
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "7 k = 2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.447,
            0.139,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "i.e.,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.415,
            0.445,
            0.538,
            0.465
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "k : 1 = 2 : 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.472,
            0.491,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You can check for the y-coordinate also."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.496,
            0.898,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the point (– 4, 6) divides the line segment joining the points A(– 6, 10) and B(3, – 8) in the ratio 2 : 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.541,
            0.899,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " You can also find this ratio by calculating the distances PA and PB and taking their ratios provided you know that A, P and B are collinear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.593,
            0.901,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 8 :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Find the coordinates of the points of trisection (i.e., points dividing in three equal parts) of the line segment joining the points A(2, – 2) and B(– 7, 4)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.639,
            0.487,
            0.703
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Let P and Q be the points of trisection of AB i.e., "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{AP} = \\mathrm{PQ} = \\mathrm{QB}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (see Fig. 7.11)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.547,
            0.641,
            0.842,
            0.684
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 18,
              "bbox": [
                0.547,
                0.641,
                0.842,
                0.684
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_10_image_18.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 19,
              "bbox": [
                0.65,
                0.684,
                0.744,
                0.703
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 7.11"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.711,
            0.9,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, P divides AB internally in the ratio 1 : 2. Therefore, the coordinates of P, by applying the section formula, are"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.235,
            0.763,
            0.645,
            0.807
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{1(-7)+2(2)}{1+2}, \\frac{1(4)+2(-2)}{1+2} \\right), \\mathrm{i.e.}, (-1,0)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.821,
            0.859,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, Q also divides AB internally in the ratio 2 : 1. So, the coordinates of Q are"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.853,
            0.651,
            0.901
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_23.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{2(-7)+1(2)}{2+1}, \\frac{2(4)+1(-2)}{2+1} \\right), \\mathrm{i.e.}, (-4, 2)"
        },
        {
